<title>USA: US to sell $30.75 bln of 2-, 5-yr notes Dec 18,190.</title>
<headline>US to sell $30.75 bln of 2-, 5-yr notes Dec 18,190.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Treasury Department said on Wednesday that it will sell $18.25 billion of 2-year notes on Dec 18 and $12.5 bln of 5-yr notes on Dec 19 to refund $27.768 billion of securities maturing Dec 31 and to raise $2.975 billion of new cash.</p>
<p>The notes will be issued Dec 31. The two-year notes mature Dec 31, 1998, and the five-year notes mature Dec 31, 2001.</p>
<p>The CUSIP number for the 2-year notes will be 9128272D3 and for the five-year notes will be 9128272E1.</p>
